{"explanation": "Within its preferred classes (mostly furry dogs and similar animals), this unit fires more when the main subject faces toward or away from the camera than when it faces right. It also fires more when the subject is sharp rather than slightly blurry. It is somewhat higher for photos with a cool blue or green tint, compared with warm-tinted or colorless ones. The tint effect rests on only 5 photos, so it is less certain. Subject size, position and horizon tilt make little difference.", "rows": [4, 24, 16, 20]}
```

